    "description": "Follow-up to #1174 (merged) — test-only, was held locally to avoid invalidating the approved head.\n\n**1. Pin the round-4 dedupe side-fix.** The '## Unreleased' append-exactly-once logic in scripts/auto_release.sh shipped untested. New sandbox test drives TWO real releases through the bare-origin fixture: after the first push, the release-tag catch-up is simulated (backdated amended bump + tag v0.1.496 + new pending work) so the coalesce window and the untagged guard both open, then the script reruns in the same sandbox. Asserts exactly one '## Unreleased' after each run and both version sections present. `AutoReleaseRun` gains `rerun()` (same-sandbox re-execution) and `originFile()` (post-run remote file reads).\n\n**2. Deflake the E1-race authorship assertion under git hooks.** The assertion failed ONLY when the suite ran inside the pre-commit gate: `git commit` exports GIT_AUTHOR_*/GIT_COMMITTER_* (the committing repo's identity) into hook processes, and scripts/ci_fast_gate.sh unsets only GIT_DIR/GIT_INDEX_FILE/GIT_WORK_TREE — the leaked vars overrode the sandbox script's own `git config user.name fa-release-bot[bot]`, so the bump came out authored as the host repo's identity. Reproduced red by exporting those vars into `dart test`; the sandbox script runs now execute with a sanitized environment (GIT_* stripped, includeParentEnvironment: false) — green with and without the leak, including under the real gate (all 9 stages OK/skip on the held commit).\n\nGates: full pre-commit suite green on this commit (test-only: flutter + integration-mock legs SKIP out-of-scope). Suite: dart test test/release_hygiene_test.dart 51/51."
  }
}

